From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] layout: Let an extension keep the stage hidden at startup

The stage is shown as soon as the system background has loaded, and the
startup animation runs before the extensions enabled at startup are
enabled: they are imported asynchronously, after the UI is built. A
session whose extension puts up its own first screen therefore shows the
overview, the top panel and the grey system background first. On a
phone that boots to VibeOS's lock screen this lasts about 6 s
(S10e: the shell starts at 8.7 s, the extension is enabled at 12.2 s,
and the lock screen's first frame is drawn at 14.65 s).

Wait for the extensions enabled at startup before showing the stage, and
add LayoutManager.holdStartup(): an extension takes a hold in enable()
and releases it once its screen is built. Until then the stage stays
hidden and the display goes on scanning out what was there before: the
boot splash Plymouth left. A hold that is never released ends 15 s after
the shell started waiting.

A startup that was held has no startup animation: the holder's screen
shows as it is. The lock screen pushes unlock-dialog, which has no
overview, so the startup would otherwise zoom the whole UI in from 75%
over the grey system background. It completes once that first frame is
on the screen. 'startup-complete' registers the display with GDM, GDM
then quits Plymouth, and the splash goes with it: completing right after
the stage is shown left the S10e black from 12.2 s to 14.2 s, while the
first frame was still being drawn. Not from the stage's 'presented'
signal, whose ClutterFrameInfo is a bare pointer GJS cannot take (each
call of the handler throws), but 100 ms after the first 'after-paint',
or after 5 s at most.

POCO X3 NFC, booted with this and VibeOS's hold: Plymouth's frame
is scanned out until 16.04 s, the lock screen from then on, nothing in
between; the display is registered at 16.15 s and Plymouth has quit by
16.19 s.

For gnome-shell-mobile 51.1.mobile.22 (tag 51.1.mobile.22 of
World/MobileShell/gnome-shell-mobile, built into /opt/gnome-mobile),
after 0003.
